From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:12:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: bind draft-token D2H copies per step

MUSA-100041. Two upstream correctness gaps in DraftTokensHandler, plus the
MUSA stream hazard they expose.

Upstream status (verified against v0.32.0, v0.33.0rc0 and v0.33.0rc1 on
2026-11-19; re-check at the next pin bump):

- A batch without structured output requests erasing drafts retained for
  in-flight structured requests is fixed upstream by 322f90a2a3 (#63219,
  per-request draft retention). That commit is not an ancestor of the v0.32.0
  pin (5df63a7203), and the same single-slot code is still present in
  v0.33.0rc1, so it landed after 2026-10-28 or is still unmerged.
- The missing retrieval on non-deferred structured+spec steps is fixed upstream
  by d5bd3d1f92 (#66081). It is not in v0.32.0 or in any v0.33 rc inspected
  here; confirm its merge state before assuming the fix is released.
- Neither upstream commit removes the single copy_stream/copy_event, so the
  MUSA per-copy stream/event binding (the shape 0141 fixed for output copies)
  is not superseded by either one.

Drop this entry only when the target pin contains both upstream commits AND
per-copy stream/event binding exists on the MUSA side. `musa_sync
upgrade-plan <new-ref> --history <full-vllm-clone>` is the mechanical check: a
MUSA entry that is already applied against the target is reported as
"already in the target: upstreamed?" for review.
